 "intro": "Judaea, 132-135 AD. Simon bar Kokhba leads a great revolt and rules as a prince. Rebels hide in caves and tunnels. You are Sextus Julius Severus, Hadrian’s best general, brought from Britain.",
 "debrief": "In Cassius Dio’s account, Severus avoided pitched battle and wore the rebels down by cutting off small groups and starving them. Rebel hiding places in caves have been found with letters of Bar Kokhba. The last stronghold, Betar, was walled in and stormed, and Bar Kokhba was killed. Losses on both sides were huge; Hadrian left out the usual 'I and the army are well' in his letter to the Senate, refounded Jerusalem as Aelia Capitolina and renamed the province. The other choices are what-ifs.",
